WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.467
-Welcome, welcome.
Thank you all for being here.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:05.234
I appreciate this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:06.934
This is clearly --
Yeah, do you just get

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:09.367
standing ovations
wherever you guys go?

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:11.534
-Yeah.

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:14.133
-It's been a while.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:15.834
I'm so happy you guys are here.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:18.934
And I know people have been
trying to get you guys together

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:20.667
to reunite for a long time.

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:21.968
Why now?

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:24.400
-Jason Reitman
wrote a great script.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.267
So full of heart
and going right back

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:29.968
to the first two movies and
its DNA and its heart and soul.

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.234
And we just read it and thought,

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:32.767
"You know,
this is the right time

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.367
and this is
the right way to do it."

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:38.234
-Jason is the son of the
original director, Ivan Reitman,

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:40.067
and Jason's made some
great movies on his own.

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:42.267
And he had his
own take on --

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:44.467
Because he grew up as a child
of the "Ghostbusters"

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:45.868
sort of in a way.

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:49.067
He had something he thought
would work as a good story,

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:51.200
and we all agreed
that he got it, yeah.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.868
-Do you remember him
as a kid on set?

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:54.968
-He was a pain in the ass.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:56.467
-Wait a second. Oh, my God.

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.634
-He was directing back then.

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:01.234
-So was his sister, Catherine.
She was a pain, too.

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.434
-Yeah, yeah, of course.
-Now they're big stars.

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:07.734
She's on "Workin' Moms."
-She directs "Workin' Moms."

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.067
And she's very good.

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:12.167
-Ernie, you're a
classically trained actor,

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:13.868
and you get on set with --

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:16.601
-Yeah, what are you
doing with us?

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:19.534
-How did you -- What did you
think about these guys?

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:22.100
Because you have
Bill, Dan, and Harold Ramis

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.567
came from a comedy background.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:24.634
-Yeah, no, it's --

00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:26.334
You know,
I'm always looking for a job,

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:28.601
so I was happy to be working.

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:31.634
But, yeah, no,
they were always very welcoming.

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:36.000
And, you know, it took a minute
to sort of catch up, I guess,

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.033
because --

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:38.200
-They knew each other, yeah.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.667
Did you get in trouble
together, you guys?

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:46.000
-Um, we had a wonderful night,
I remember,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.501
where we had available to us
some New York police motorcycles

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:51.400
because we were shooting Uptown.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.067
And, so, Billy and I decided
we'd would like to take

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:56.267
a little ride around
Central Park.

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:59.267
And we grabbed those bikes
and screamed all over the park.

00:01:59.267 --> 00:02:01.033
It was closed for some reason.

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:02.934
And we were just --
You know, lights and sirens

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:05.300
and, you know,
pulling over pedestrians.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.133
-Well, we were helping out,
you know.

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:09.367
-Oh, wow.
-That's right, yeah.

00:02:09.367 --> 00:02:10.434
-That's very thoughtful
of you guys.

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:11.934
-You know, auxiliary.

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:14.133
You know,
kind of like volunteers.

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:15.434
-That's so thoughtful.

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:17.367
And, Ernie, what do you
do when that happens?

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.000
Do you just let it ride?

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.334
-Yeah, I just ride.
I just watch.

00:02:21.334 --> 00:02:22.801
-You sit back.
-You know, I'm here, yeah.

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:26.434
-Bill and Dan, this building,
I know, means a lot to you.

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:27.801
This is where you
got your start,

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:29.234
"Saturday Night Live."

00:02:29.234 --> 00:02:30.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
I mean, a lot of -- Basically.

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:32.667
I know you...

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:34.701
-And still going.
-And still going.

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:36.701
-With great people
and great writing.

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:39.000
And this season,
they're really hitting it.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.267
-I remember, Dan,
when I first started,

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:42.400
you came into the office.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.567
And I just even
heard your voice,

00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:46.234
and I was like,
"That's Dan Aykroyd."

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:48.968
You just hear Dan Aykroyd's
voice through the office.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.467
You're like,
"You're the new kid?"

00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:52.133
You're like, "Come with me.
I'll show you around."

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:53.868
And he took me
to the 11th floor.

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:55.100
-Mm-hmm.
-We crawled --

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.501
-We went through a window
and went to the garden.

00:02:57.501 --> 00:02:59.033
-Yeah, we crawled
through a window

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:00.300
and ended up in the garden.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.434
-Yeah. That's right.

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:02.467
You can go to the 11th floor.

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:03.968
And you pass
the secretary's desk,

00:03:03.968 --> 00:03:05.200
and she goes, "What are you..."

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.634
And you go through
the window next to her desk

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:07.868
and you're out on the
roof garden overlooking

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:09.701
St. Patrick's Cathedral
and all that.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:11.234
-Did you used to hang there?

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:13.133
-Well, you were helping out,
and I appreciate that.

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:15.133
-Yeah, I was.
I was just helping out.

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:16.300
That's all I was doing.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.801
-Like, you couldn't believe
that there was --

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:20.667
Why would anybody be in the
elevator when you could be on

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.901
this beautiful
garden overlooking St. Pat's?

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:25.133
You know, it was pretty nice.
-Can you still go up there?

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:26.334
I think they might have
closed it.

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:27.868
-Yeah, you can still
do everything.

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:30.000
-Yeah. It's still there.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.701
-You just got to have
a little key.

00:03:31.701 --> 00:03:34.000
-Yeah.
-Unlock the window or break it.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.300
Because they repair
everything around here.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.334
It's great.

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:39.501
-Dan, can you talk about
"Ghostbusters,"

00:03:39.501 --> 00:03:41.501
where the idea came from?

00:03:41.501 --> 00:03:43.567
-Well, you know,
my great-grandfather Sam

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:46.200
was a dentist up there in
Kingston, Ontario.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.434
So, sometimes, with not much to
do in the winter.

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:51.300
he began to research
spiritualism in the 1920s.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.701
And he was really into
the concept of

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:54.901
the idea of mediumship,

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.968
that the consciousness survives
after death.

00:03:56.968 --> 00:03:58.167
Not only the soul,

00:03:58.167 --> 00:03:59.868
but the consciousness
survives after death.

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:02.133
So, he had all these journals
sitting around the house.

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:04.267
And I was sitting in the
old séance room

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.567
one afternoon in the summer
and I was reading some of

00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:09.767
the journals that he was writing
and I just thought,

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:12.200
"You know, would it be good to
do an old-style

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.701
Bob Hope, Bing Crosby,
Abbott and Costello,

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:16.868
Bowery Boys-style comedy,

00:04:16.868 --> 00:04:18.334
like they used to do
in the '30s?"

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:20.934
You know, ghost breakers and
ghost chasers.

00:04:20.934 --> 00:04:22.968
And I thought if
you used all of the research

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:25.367
that's really been done and
combined it together,

00:04:25.367 --> 00:04:26.734
we could have something there.

00:04:26.734 --> 00:04:29.067
Now, no one knew what
ectoplasm was

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:30.834
before the
"Ghostbusters" movie, right?

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:33.634
Now millions of people know
what ectoplasm is now.

00:04:33.634 --> 00:04:36.434
And all over the country now,
in every county,

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:38.467
there is a ghost-busting society
with the equipment.

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:39.534
They go out.

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:40.601
There's all kinds of shows of

00:04:40.601 --> 00:04:42.100
the paranormal
and the supernatural.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.400
That's all from my
great-grandfather's work

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.133
and the movie
we all put together.

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:48.567
I believe that's true.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.567 --> 00:04:50.701
-That's fantastic.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.501
-Dan, this is
late-night television.

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:57.667
People are going to look for a
number on the lower third

00:04:57.667 --> 00:05:00.234
of the screen here to call
about this thing.

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:02.934
You don't say that kind of stuff
late at night.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.534
-Dan, was it true that
the script was like

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:07.534
300 pages or something?

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:08.901
-It wasn't. No, it was about --

00:05:08.901 --> 00:05:10.300
-900 pages.
-Thank you, Bill.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:13.100
-No, it was about --
That was the other script.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.334
This one was about 150.

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:18.601
And, you know, it had ecto.
It had Stay-Puft.

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:20.901
It had the packs.
It had the concept.

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:23.534
It just -- It was --
It took place

00:05:23.534 --> 00:05:25.767
in another dimension,
rather than our dimension.

00:05:25.767 --> 00:05:28.200
And, so, it was Harold and Ivan
that sort of said,

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.501
"Let's get it to something
that we know.

00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:32.334
Let's get it to something
we can identify with."

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:34.267
And that's ghostbusting in
New York City.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:35.968
But all of the elements were
in the first script

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.968
that we eventually
ended up using.

00:05:37.968 --> 00:05:39.901
Yeah.
-Sorry. That made me laugh.

00:05:39.901 --> 00:05:42.400
-"Ghostbusting in
New York City."

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:44.501
-"How about we do it on Earth?"
Yeah, that's a great idea.

00:05:44.501 --> 00:05:45.901
-Well, that was it, you see?

00:05:45.901 --> 00:05:47.367
-Something we all know --

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:49.467
ghostbusting here in the
Tri-State Area.

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:51.100
-Yeah.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:52.434
Yeah.

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:54.467
-The name "Ghostbusters" wasn't
originally -- Right?

00:05:54.467 --> 00:05:55.534
It wasn't cleared or --

00:05:55.534 --> 00:05:56.634
-We called the movie
"Ghostbusters,"

00:05:56.634 --> 00:05:58.467
but there was a show on
Taft Broadcasting

00:05:58.467 --> 00:06:00.434
with Larry Storch.

00:06:00.434 --> 00:06:02.000
Remember from "F Troop"?
-Yes, of course.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.367
-And Forrest Tucker? Yeah.

00:06:05.367 --> 00:06:06.801
And it was called
"Ghost Busters."

00:06:06.801 --> 00:06:10.133
And they had a gorilla that went
around busting ghosts, you know.

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:11.434
-I love that.

00:06:11.434 --> 00:06:14.067
-It wasn't like the technology
that we had or anything,

00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:15.067
but it was just the title.

00:06:15.067 --> 00:06:17.234
So we had to pay
to get the title.

00:06:17.234 --> 00:06:18.467
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:18.467 --> 00:06:19.901
-Actually,
you brought a clip of --

00:06:19.901 --> 00:06:22.000
This is Dan, Bill,
and Harold Ramis

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.467
shooting a scene for
"Ghostbusters"

00:06:23.467 --> 00:06:25.501
before you settled on
the name "Ghostbusters."

00:06:25.501 --> 00:06:26.767
Look at this.

00:06:26.767 --> 00:06:29.033
-Are you troubled by
strange noises in the night?

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:31.968
-Do you experience feelings of
dread in your basement or attic?

00:06:31.968 --> 00:06:33.834
-Have you or
any of your family ever seen

00:06:33.834 --> 00:06:35.434
a spook, specter, or ghost?

00:06:35.434 --> 00:06:37.133
-If the answer is "yes,"
then don't wait another minute.

00:06:37.133 --> 00:06:39.434
Pick up your phone
and call the professionals.

00:06:39.434 --> 00:06:41.100
-Ghost-stoppers!

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:44.234
-Take 4.
-Take 4!

00:06:44.234 --> 00:06:45.934
-If the answer is "yes,"
then don't wait another minute.

00:06:45.934 --> 00:06:48.133
Pick up your phone
and call the professionals.

00:06:48.133 --> 00:06:49.567
-Ghost-blasters!

00:06:49.567 --> 00:06:52.234
-Yeah. Ghost-blasters!

00:06:52.234 --> 00:06:54.133
When we come back,
we're going to talk about

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:55.467
"Ghostbusters: Afterlife."

00:06:55.467 --> 00:06:58.033
More with Bill Murray,
Dan Aykroyd, Ernie Hudson!

00:06:58.033 --> 00:07:00.100
Come on back!
♪♪

00:07:10.634 --> 00:07:14.300
-♪ In the cool of the evening ♪

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:19.234
♪ When everything is
feelin' kind of groovy ♪

00:07:19.234 --> 00:07:23.567
♪ And I call you up and ask you
if you want to come and

00:07:23.567 --> 00:07:27.801
come and see a movie ♪

00:07:27.801 --> 00:07:30.634
♪ Well, first, you say "no" ♪

00:07:30.634 --> 00:07:32.567
♪ You got plans for the night ♪

00:07:32.567 --> 00:07:36.934
♪ And then you stop
and say "alright" ♪

00:07:36.934 --> 00:07:39.868
♪ Oh, kinda spooky ♪

00:07:39.868 --> 00:07:41.634
♪ With a spooky
little girl like you ♪

